{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_30465d4a86544b139d318171e7d86941","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b95173defbe87c48","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\n# 4 distinct stem types, each 8bp, mutually non-cross-complementary\n# Type1 GC stem: 5'=GGGGCCCC paired with 3'=GGGGCCCC? need 3' revcomp of 5'\n# stem 5' half S, 3' half = revcomp(S). For 8bp stem, 5' half is 4nt, 3' half 4nt.\n# Use 4 types with distinct 4-mers, none revcomp of another.\ntypes = {\n 1: 'GGGG'+'CCCC',  # 5'GGGG 3'CCCC (revcomp of GGGG = CCCC) ok self\n 2: 'AAAA'+'UUUU',\n 3: 'GAGA'+'CUCU',  # revcomp(GAGA)=UCUC -> need 3' = UCUC, but written 5'->3' the 3'half of stem... \n}\n# Actually for a hairpin: positions 0-7 stem 5'->3', then loop, then positions 12-19 stem 3'->5' read 5'->3'.\n# Pairing: pos0 with pos19, pos7 with pos12. So seq[0..7] pairs with seq[12..19] reversed.\n# If 5'half = seq[0..7], 3'half = seq[12..19], then seq[12+k] pairs with seq[7-k].\n# For complementary: seq[7-k] complement = seq[12+k]. \n# Simplest: seq[0..7]=s, seq[12..19]=revcomp(s). \n# To prevent cross-hairpin pairing between hairpin i 5'half and hairpin j 3'half:\n#   s_i should not be revcomp(revcomp(s_j)) = s_j... wait.\n#   HP i 5'half s_i pairs with HP j 3'half revcomp(s_j) iff s_i = revcomp(revcomp(s_j)) = s_j. \n#   So identical 5'halves always cross-pair! Need distinct 5'halves where s_i != s_j.\n# But also s_i pairs with revcomp(s_j): s_i complement-reverse = revcomp(s_j)? \n#   A stretch s_i pairs with stretch t (antiparallel) iff t = revcomp(s_i).\n#   HP j 3'half = revcomp(s_j). So s_i pairs with HP j 3'half iff revcomp(s_j)=revcomp(s_i) iff s_j=s_i.\n# So distinct 5'halves => no cross pairing between 5' and 3' halves. \n# But s_i could pair with HP j 5'half s_j if revcomp(s_j)=s_i i.e. s_j=revcomp(s_i). Avoid that too.\n# Pick 8 distinct 4-mers, none being revcomp of another, all self-revcomp-free set.\nimport itertools\ndef revcomp(s):\n    comp={'G':'C','C':'G','A':'U','U':'A'}\n    return ''.join(comp[c] for c in reversed(s))\nbases='GCAU'\nquads=[''.join(p) for p in itertools.product(bases,repeat=4)]\n# choose set of 8 quads, no two revcomp of each other\nchosen=[]\nused=set()\nfor q in quads:\n    if q in used: continue\n    rc=revcomp(q)\n    if q==rc: continue  # skip self-revcomp (palindrome) to allow distinct halves\n    chosen.append(q)\n    used.add(q); used.add(rc)\n    if len(chosen)>=8: break\nprint(chosen)\nprint([revcomp(q) for q in chosen])\n\"","description":"Pick 8 distinct stem halves"}}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.2","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38795fad-543f-4d31-b95a-fb482773ebd1","uuid":"35c6a666-4c92-4933-8639-aeb5d72572d7"}
